<description>&lt;p&gt;Algeria has deployed troops into Niger to protect energy interests, adding a state actor to the conflict. Armed terrorists are reported crossing the Kaduna River toward Shiroro in Niger State, indicating a new movement of fighters. Journalists continue to face impunity, with 12 of 13 killed since 2006 still without justice. The conflict also sees ongoing kidnappings of Islamic school students and a dynamite explosion linked to smugglers moving explosives to Burkina Faso. The UCDP recorded 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxOd1NKTllUNTJiakU5RGdaNFRwekM3SnNaeC1tUGw0QWNvOGNsVkI2SkpPVFlXNDlKR3FSTTBvTTRDdVpTbk93YnVmVjIzencyVmxUN3BZRmdGQ1EwcXZSTW5sUTdGQTROZHpFZ1ByY2wzdzRlMWlmZjA3T05xcGx6MHQ1TEZqU3Zvc1kw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sri Lanka Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTFBGT1RjejE5QkpYMlJkRm01ZWVLeWlBbnNtdGVBRUFVSHM1NXdPSnBPaDBfOWdqdklIVnZyNTBsOHR0YzZZZHlJcEhPcy05a1N6UFJfcHM4b29zbndoM0HSAWNBVV95cUxPc3BzWlV6ZXZyZkNSbzAwSzRGTmtiNkRsUEtKVWhxNXhkaUZkRThMa2owUVU4eGVOMnNqamY1TFBaTWNCSUYxTzF0ZG1Tb1I2bFNOb01DMTByczVoMG13MFdhUDg?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE5oT2RKWWJoT2VJVi0xcnlZWXFiMVZtUXVFUmF1VHBXTVZVRGtnQmplWU00XzZVZHJVRmVubWRGY3NEOFlZVnNCVTM5cTczc05CX21QUlg2OHRBY1p1?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE9kVDMta3ZRUm10bTZPSXNGeWljSnYwQnVZMnNHN1lXLUxqM1YzVVBxTUhwMHVQMkdPdmhzYXlDSU1FcUhSSEhoYi0tWTZnTVdTRVVmNEFDVjVQMmtj?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPX2VVeXlGWHIwUFQxZTJReXFma1M1UHhIN1JLcjJfRElwT21wZ3d0cEs5dTNtQ1lmV1d1b3dqS2kxRnJFYzhtTjMzeEtsdjJjTVhkNTFXMVNJTGhlbUw2OVRiMVptZmpRekRjSjg0RUJuTWF